==German==

===Etymology===
{{compound|Eisen|Bahn|lang=de}}, originally for the iron rails of trains used in mining.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈaɪ̯zənˌbaːn/|[ˈaɪ̯zənˌbaːn]|[ˈaɪ̯zn̩ˌbaːn]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Eisenbahn.ogg|Audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-Eisenbahn.ogg|Audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{hyphenation|Ei|sen|bahn|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f}}

# [[railway]], [[railroad]] {{gloss|transporting system}}
#: ''Die '''Eisenbahn''' war die erste Verkehrsrevolution.''
#:: The '''railway''' was the first revolution of traffic.
# {{lb|de|somewhat|informal}} [[train]]
#: ''Da hinten kommt eine '''Eisenbahn'''!''
#:: There’s a '''train''' approaching over there!

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|railway}} {{l|de|Schienenverkehr}}
* {{sense|train}} {{l|de|Zug}}

